{
 "exercise": "adv-94",
 "unit": "unit16-advanced",
 "title": "94: FSOP (File Stream Oriented Programming)",
 "desc": "Goal: Execute the most advanced FILE exploitation technique — File Stream Oriented Programming. FSOP chains heap corruption with the FILE structure linked list to achieve arbitrary code execution through __overflow.How FSOP works:1. glibc maintains a linked list of all FILE streams via _IO_list_all (a global pointer).2. On abort() or exit(), glibc calls _IO_flush_all_lockp(), which walks _IO_list_all and calls __overflow on each FILE whose write pointer (_IO_write_ptr) exceeds its write base (_IO_write_base).3. If you corrupt the unsorted bin (via heap overflow/UAF), a failed malloc triggers malloc_printerr -> abort() -> _IO_flush_all_lockp().4. By placing a crafted fake FILE structure at a known address and linking it via the unsorted bin attack (overwriting _IO_list_all), you control the vtable pointer. When __overflow is called, it jumps to your address.Key constraints for triggering __overflow:fp->_IO_write_ptr > fp->_IO_write_base (forces the flush path)fp->_mode  (avoids wide-char path)fp->__vtable->__overflow = winOverflow the buffer to overwrite the return address with win(), modeling the FSOP control-flow hijack.",
 "source": [
  "// FSOP: File Stream Oriented Programming",
  "// _IO_list_all -> stdout -> stderr -> ...",
  "",
  "// On abort()/exit():",
  "//   _IO_flush_all_lockp() walks _IO_list_all",
  "//   For each FILE: if _IO_write_ptr > _IO_write_base",
  "//     -> call vtable->__overflow(fp, EOF)",
  "",
  "// Attack chain:",
  "// 1. Corrupt unsorted bin -> overwrite _IO_list_all",
  "// 2. _IO_list_all now points to crafted fake FILE",
  "// 3. Fake FILE has: write_ptr > write_base",
  "// 4. Fake FILE->vtable->__overflow = win()",
  "// 5. Trigger abort() via corrupted heap -> BOOM",
  "",
  "void win() { printf(\"FLAG\\n\"); }",
  "",
  "void vuln() {",
  "    char buf[16];",
  "    // heap setup: unsorted bin attack",
  "    gets(buf);",
  "    // Triggers: malloc_printerr -> abort()",
  "    // -> _IO_flush_all_lockp()",
  "    // -> fake_file->vtable->__overflow()",
  "    // -> win()!",
  "}",
  "",
  "// Fake FILE structure layout:",
  "// _flags      = 0x00000000",
  "// _IO_write_ptr = 0x1  (must be > write_base)",
  "// _IO_write_base = 0x0",
  "// _mode       = 0x0  (must be <= 0)",
  "// __vtable    = &fake_vtable",
  "// fake_vtable.__overflow = win"
 ],
